// A **positional** variant payload (`Leaf(Widget)`) names a type, and that name is validated like
// every other annotation — an unresolvable one is E0013.
//
// It is spelled unlike every other annotation, though: a positional payload is parsed with its type
// as the field's *name* and no annotation at all, so the declaration walk's "check the annotation"
// step saw nothing and this was the one type position in the language nobody validated. The named
// form `Leaf(item: Widget)` was correctly rejected while this one checked clean.
// expect: error E0013 at 11:10
// expect: exit 1
enum Tree {
    Leaf(Widget);
    Nil;
}

echo 1;
